Prompt:

[PRODUCT / MATERIAL]: {red wine / coffee / sparkling water / ink / ...}
[BRAND]: {brand name}
[PRODUCT NAME]: {product name}
[CONTAINER]: {bottle / pouch / can / dropper / ...}
[PALETTE]: {background + liquid + typography colors}
[LIQUID BEHAVIOR]: {splash / bubbles / swirl / diffusion / refraction / ...}
[INFO TEXT]: {2–4 short product lines}
[FORMAT]: 9:16 vertical

Create a refined experimental typography poster where letters behave like real physical objects interacting with liquid.

Place the {CONTAINER} near the top edge, partially cropped and tilted downward. Let letters from {BRAND} and {PRODUCT NAME} pour out, fall through generous negative space, and enter {PRODUCT / MATERIAL}.

Give the falling letters controlled randomness through varied scale, rotation, spacing, overlap and depth. Keep a clear downward motion, with the type becoming denser near the liquid surface.

Make the liquid boundary the main visual event. As letters enter the liquid, apply {LIQUID BEHAVIOR} through realistic refraction, bubbles, drag, partial occlusion, distortion or fluid diffusion. Some letters can cross the surface, with their underwater portions visibly affected by the medium.

Follow a clear visual rhythm:

release → fall → gather → impact → transform

Keep splashes elegant and restrained. Use transparent and concentrated liquid layers, subtle depth, and visible negative space rather than heavy fluid effects.

Use {PALETTE} to create a slight contrast between the upper air space and lower liquid space. Add only a small editorial information area using {INFO TEXT}.

Overall look: minimal, premium, editorial, experimental, physically believable and detailed up close while remaining clear at thumbnail size.

Avoid heavy 3D type, random scattered letters, excessive copy, oversized splashes, clutter, or generic commercial-ad styling.

Prompt:

【POSTER TITLE】{e.g. RIVER OF LIGHT}  
【SUBTITLE】{short poetic sentence}  
【LANDSCAPE】{mountain valley / gorge / river / basin / cliffs}  
【MOOD】{twilight / moonlit / quiet / monumental / mysterious}  
【COLOR PALETTE】{deep blue, black, teal, warm ivory, burnt orange}  
【SMALL TEXT】{series name / field study / archive / year}

Create a 9:16 vertical English landscape poster built primarily through flowing contour linework and bold color.

Design the landscape first with strong, simple, readable landforms: monumental mountains, cliffs, valleys, rivers, ridges, forests or open terrain. The composition must remain visually powerful even at thumbnail size.

Use long, continuous lines to describe the structure and volume of the landscape. Mountain lines should follow slopes, ridges and geological folds; rivers and paths should create natural visual movement; sky lines should be calmer, longer and more horizontal. The linework must feel directional and intentional rather than random hatching or decorative noise.

Use a bold but controlled palette. Combine deep ink black and dark blue landforms with glacier blue, muted teal and warm ivory linework. Add small areas of burnt orange or copper along selected ridges, terrain edges or vegetation to create strong contrast and visual energy.

Keep the main shapes dark and graphic, then use line density and color shifts to create depth. Avoid excessive micro-detail, distressed texture, messy cross-hatching, neon effects or generic fantasy lighting.

Integrate refined editorial typography directly into the composition. Use an elegant high-contrast serif for the main title, supported by smaller modern text. The typography should feel like an art publication or exhibition poster, not a travel advertisement.

Use only meaningful text related to the poster concept. Do not add random slogans, filler copy, fake coordinates, meaningless labels, logos, Chinese characters or watermarks.

The final result should feel like a complete collectible artwork — part topographic drawing, part printmaking, part contemporary editorial poster design.

Prompt:

【Series Name】: {e.g. FOCAL IDENTITY}  
【Main Title】: {e.g. MOTION / OBSERVE / SIGNAL / FRAME}  
【Subject】: {age, gender, identity, profession}  
【Name】: {name}  
【Role】: {profession / creative role}  
【Key Line】: {short concept-driven sentence}  
【Accent Color】: {yellow / red / cobalt blue / rust orange}  
【Focus Method】: {horizontal sharp slice / floating focus window / vertical sharp slice / offset focus frame}  
【Aspect Ratio】: 9:16

Create a sophisticated editorial portrait poster built around selective focus. Use a realistic photographic portrait with natural skin texture, pores, subtle imperfections, believable hair, and authentic facial structure. Avoid plastic skin, CGI smoothness, heavy beauty retouching, or generic commercial-model styling.

Keep most of the portrait softly blurred, slightly motion-softened, desaturated, or reduced in detail. Only the selected 【Focus Method】 should return to sharp detail, natural skin tone, and clear texture. The sharp and blurred areas must remain perfectly aligned as the same person and the same photographic moment, with no duplicated eyes, second face, or pasted-photo effect.

Choose one focus structure: a horizontal sharp band across the eyes, a small floating window isolating part of the face, a narrow vertical sharp slice through motion blur, or a larger offset frame that deliberately shifts attention away from the facial center.

Use a restrained neutral palette of charcoal, gray, warm beige, off-white, and natural skin tones. Use 【Accent Color】 as the only strong accent for the focus lines, main title, and a few key details. Keep the visual rule: Neutral Field + One Accent Color.

Use mature magazine-style typography: a high-contrast editorial serif for 【Main Title】, a condensed bold sans serif for 【Name】 and 【Role】, and a small neutral sans serif for secondary information. Include 【Key Line】 as meaningful copy connected to the subject and concept, not random filler text.

Keep the composition asymmetric with generous negative space. Let the portrait, typography, and focus geometry interact naturally. Add subtle film grain, light scan texture, and restrained print texture so the whole poster feels like one finished editorial piece.

The final result should feel like a polished independent fashion, photography, music, or culture magazine poster, with blur and sharpness deliberately controlling where the viewer looks.

Avoid cyberpunk HUDs, excessive UI graphics, neon gradients, gibberish text, logos, watermarks, numbering, sparkle symbols, harsh Gaussian blur, melted facial features, duplicated features, plastic skin, and over-retouching.

提示词：

【古诗词】{标题、作者、原文}
【核心场景】{填写或由AI提取}
【关键意象】{填写或由AI提取}
【视觉关系】{如红杏越墙、蜻蜓立荷、牧童指路}
【主色调】{填写东方传统配色}
【画幅比例】9:16

根据古诗词创作一张新中式细线设色装饰插画海报，将诗中的景物、动作与情绪转化为具有明确视觉叙事的东方场景。

采用高位俯瞰、东方散点透视与现代平面构成。树冠呈柔软蓬松的云团状色块，边缘带有细腻粉末点染质感，内部穿插纤细连续的墨黑枝条。建筑采用精细工笔线描、青绿瓦片、暖白墙面与朱红木结构。

人物、动物和植物使用统一的精细线描与平面设色，动作自然，结构准确，主体之间的空间关系清楚。

地面与水面以暖米白大面积留白表现，辅以少量墨色阴影与简洁细线。构图根据诗词灵活变化，突出核心意象，保持主次清晰、疏密有序。

色彩采用石青、石绿、黛青、朱砂、赭红、象牙白等东方传统色系，设色饱满均匀、哑光干净，保留轻微纸本质感。

加入大幅暖白色中文标题、小型纵排原诗句、作者署名和少量朱印，形成完整的东方文化艺术海报。

避免写实摄影、3D、动漫、浓重水墨、油画厚涂、复杂背景、过度颗粒和人工做旧。

